{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1511280-trinity-fan-theories","id":1511280,"title":"Trinity Fan Theories","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-10T14:11:13-07:00","id":1511280,"title":"Trinity Fan Theories","content":"Random Ideas ramblings of fans. \ud83d\ude0e <br /> <br /> 1. <b>Aeon era - Section Minerva from Trinity Aeon is Pharaohs Lightkeepers of previous eras</b> <br /> Secretive bunch? Check. Using stealth? Check. Having symbol of Lighthouse? Check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T20:47:20-07:00","id":1511325,"title":"","content":"I'm fond of the theory that Michael Mercer is actually the hybrid clone baby of extradimensional versions of Max Mercer and Michael Donighal. Maybe the two of them had some sort of relationship, or maybe Dr. Primoris was trying to use a child to make a relationship work. Given his belief that he and Max were the two most 'evolved' Inspired, I could see him wanting to combine their traits in a 'perfect' baby. An adult Mike Mercer became a talent and set out across realities to find his own place in the multiverse, eventually succeeding the local version of Max as head of Aeon.<br /> <br /> This makes sense to me for several reasons.<br /> <br /> 1). Mike Mercer is unlikely to be a future or near parallel version of Max since he eventually had a daughter, even though Max is asexual. Unless Margaret Mercer was either a test tube baby or adopted, Mike isn't Max. She also calls Max grandfather, meaning she knows the two of them as independent beings.<br /> <br /> 2). Mike Mercer seems like a young man when he introduces himself to Max, meaning he was presumably born after the Hammersmith Event. Since I can't picture asexual Max Mercer having a kid with an unnamed woman so soon after rejecting Mike Donighal's declaration of love, that means Max didn't literally father Mike. A super science baby makes as much sense as anything else, and more sense than many other options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T19:06:59-07:00","id":1513147,"title":"","content":"I thought Michael was a younger Maxwell that time traveled from the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T21:42:50-07:00","id":1513263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Planguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1511280-trinity-fan-theories?p=1513147#post1513147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Michael was a younger Maxwell that time traveled from the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was mentioned as one rumor about his origin, but seems unlikely since Michael's personality is significantly different from Max's. As I mentioned in my previous post, Michael also went on to have a daughter (Margaret Mercer, who ran Aeon during the nova era), while Max is asexual. Unless she's either adopted or a test tube baby, Michael isn't asexual.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T20:52:48-07:00","id":1513353,"title":"","content":"Oh? When was it stated Maxwell was asexual? That seems an unnecessary addition to his character considering it is established that he has a granddaughter. Maxwell doesn't seem the type to feel the need to force himself to have a child just to meet societal expectations. If he didn't feel the need to have a romantic relationship I don't see why he would ever have children. His organization and his various charities would be more then enough for his legacy.<br /> <br /> I don't doubt Onyx Path would add this to his character for the sake of representation but this is an aspect of his character that is firmly going into the dustbin in my timeline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T06:23:02-07:00","id":1513385,"title":"","content":"Y\u2019all understand a lot of different folks fall under the asexual umbrella and it\u2019s fairly common for Ace people to have kids right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T14:41:11-07:00","id":1513454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Planguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1511280-trinity-fan-theories?p=1513353#post1513353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh? When was it stated Maxwell was asexual? That seems an unnecessary addition to his character considering it is established that he has a granddaughter. Maxwell doesn't seem the type to feel the need to force himself to have a child just to meet societal expectations. If he didn't feel the need to have a romantic relationship I don't see why he would ever have children. His organization and his various charities would be more then enough for his legacy.<br /> <br /> I don't doubt Onyx Path would add this to his character for the sake of representation but this is an aspect of his character that is firmly going into the dustbin in my timeline.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can want to have children without wanting a romantic relationship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T18:40:03-07:00","id":1513493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Planguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1511280-trinity-fan-theories?p=1513353#post1513353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh? When was it stated Maxwell was asexual? That seems an unnecessary addition to his character considering it is established that he has a granddaughter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the change was made because the 1E situation where gay Mike Donighal loved straight Max Mercer, but his love wasn't reciprocated was felt to be too cliche. Having Max genuinely return that love but still refusing a relationship due to being asexual was an interesting new twist.<br /> <br /> I personally find the idea of macho Errol Flynn-style action icon Max Mercer being asexual to be an interesting take on the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}